	(text "WS (GPIO16), ADD8 (GPIO14) and OSC_PICO (GPIO22) are open-drain:\nthe Pico drives them low or releases them, never high. R20, R19 and\nR25 (on the top sheet) pull them up to +5V; these pins are 5 V tolerant.\nKeep the internal pull-downs off (RP2350-E9). ADD8 is released during\na Load Address, so the TMS5220 drives it freely.\nU3 takes T11 and I/O directly: their negative swing is held by\nU3's input clamp diodes, well inside the 50 mA clamp rating."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6b44f372-972f-4e14-86e1-60fcea59e698")
	)
	(text "I2S output to a PCM5102A board (11-pin header).\nGPIO20 BCK and GPIO21 LCK are consecutive for the PIO I2S program.\nSCL grounded: the PCM5102A clocks itself from BCK (internal PLL).\nFLT, DMP and FMT low: normal filter, no de-emphasis, I2S format.\nXMT tied to the board's own 3.3V output (unmuted).\nVCC from +5V via the board's regulators."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.55 60.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e1e6da5a-ddd2-4821-96ce-d816aa393e1f")
	)
